# Wave W17-T (Route 132): stream sand — current-edge sand: a bright shore sand at the first current road\u2019s edge, foam-streak flecks standing in loose east-running streaks across the tread — the current\u2019s foam combing the shore sand as the sea begins to run in rivers (design: foam-streaked current bands running W-E like a river laid on the sea; the shipped current cells themselves are mechanic data, byte-identical entire — the sand kind carries only the shore\u2019s answer to the foam). Route 132\u2019s own sand — the gentlest of the three current shores: split from Route 133\u2019s rapid sand by foam hardness (loose streaks vs hard dashes) and from Route 131\u2019s rope-worn mooring sand by the streaks\u2019 direction (the sea\u2019s work, not the rafts\u2019).
